There is no network “split” between 20.x (OSPF side) and 120.x (EIGRP side): end-to-end reachability is intact. However, one half of the two‑way redistribution at the OSPF–EIGRP boundary is missing. The affected component is FRR EIGRP on r11 (the boundary router), specifically the absence of OSPF-to-EIGRP redistribution.

